  "metadata": {
    "title": "Daily electricity demand data for Indian states (2014\u20132024)",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.14983362",
    "publication_date": "2025-03-06",
    "description": "<p>These files contain data scraped from India's national grid, organised as follows:<br><br>daily_energy_met_MU: the total electricity supplied by the grid to each state in units of MU (GWh), daily aggregates<br>peak_met_MW: the peak power supplied to each state (per day, in units of MW)<br>peak_unmet_MW: the maximum deficit in supplied power (compared to demand) for each state (per day, in units of MW)</p>\n<p>Corrected versions of the above are also supplied, which have undergone a simple quality control that checks for transcription errors. We recommend using these unless you intend to conduct your own quality control.</p>\n<p>Individual state files contain relevant meteorological data for each state (for training ML demand models). These include daily minima, means, and maxima for the following: 2-m temperautre, 10-m u and v winds, 2-m dewpoint temperature, surface solar radiation, total cloud cover, and UTCI.</p>\n<p>For more information on the methodology and use of these data, see our paper: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/388109973_Building_and_explaining_data-driven_energy_demand_models_for_Indian_states</p>",
    "access_right": "open",
